UserEvent{userId=SAV2001, type=TRANSFER, amount=50000}
```

### What should a senior engineer know?

Keying by userId concentrates a hot user on one partition; mitigate with salting if needed. Manual-ack must always acknowledge on both the success and the DLT paths or the partition stalls. Batch mode needs partial-failure handling: filter bad records to the DLT and process the rest. Pausing is healthier than letting a listener fail repeatedly against a dead dependency.

```text
# Senior checklist:
# 1. Key by userId -> consistent partition -> ordered per user
# 2. MANUAL ack -> offset advances only after success
# 3. Bounded retries + DLT -> poison pills handled
# 4. Batch mode -> bulk DB write -> one commit
# 5. Pause/resume -> downstream-aware flow control
# 6. Idempotent processing -> at-least-once is safe
```
